; Regression test for issue #3313: inside a commodity block, a ';'
; outside quotes also ends the symbol of an alias or a format and
; begins a comment.  An alias used to keep its comment, registering
; "POUND ; old name" rather than POUND, and since the fix for #2872 a
; commented format line was rejected ("unexpected characters ';' after
; commodity symbol in format directive"), although 3.4.1 accepted it.

commodity GBP
    alias POUND ; old name
    format GBP 1,000.00 ; two decimals, thousands separated

; Quotes keep a ';' in the symbol; the comment starts after them.
commodity "N4; foo"
    alias "N4 ALIAS";an alias with a space
    format 1000.000 "N4; foo";three decimals

; Stripping the comment leaves a multi-word alias whole.
commodity CAD
    alias Canadian Dollar ; no quotes needed

2024/01/01 Test
    Assets:Cash    1234.567 POUND
    Assets:Cash    1234.5 "N4 ALIAS"
    Assets:Cash    10 "Canadian Dollar"
    Equity

test bal --flat Assets
              10 CAD
        GBP 1,234.57
    1234.500 N4; foo  Assets:Cash
end test
